content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22871, on the chemically dosed filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable manufacturer criterion is Figure 3, for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The reported 7.6 mm/s at the drive-end bearing housing is above the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary and within Zone D (7.1 to 11.0 mm/s), labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. Zone C's plan-maintenance response therefore does not apply; stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing temperature: the applicable limits are for the bearing-housing surface. Normal is up to 70 C, alarm is 80 C, and trip is 90 C. The reported 84 C is above both the normal and alarm limits but below the 90 C trip limit. SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift when the manufacturer's alarm limit is exceeded; the immediate stop is separately required by the Zone D vibration reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-area leakage: approximately one drop per second confirms the manual's 'Leakage at shaft seal' symptom. No numerical allowable leakage rate is provided, so this reading cannot be compared with a numerical leak-rate limit. The manual's corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal and check alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry running: the HF-300 has Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and the explicit operating limit is 'never run dry'. The reported approximately 10-minute dry run exceeded that limit. Seal run dry is a documented probable cause of shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal damage, including worn or cracked seal faces caused or worsened by the 10-minute dry run, is the leading explanation for the shaft-area dripping.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the original HF3-450 component seal is installed, its documented early-failure mechanism is also credible: SB-2026-014 attributes early failures on pumps from serial HF3-22000 to a revised sleeve tolerance. P-104's serial HF3-22871 is within that range.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment could contribute to all three principal findings: seal leakage, high vibration, and high bearing temperature. Alignment must therefore be checked.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is a possible cause of the high vibration and bearing temperature; over-greasing is a separate documented possible cause of the high bearing temperature. Inspect the bearings and check grease quantity.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation/NPSH problems, are additional documented possible causes of the high vibration; inspect the impeller and check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-104 immediately for Zone D vibration. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart. Handle this work order as P1 within the shift because the 84 C bearing-housing temperature exceeds the 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. Isolate and drain the pump in accordance with mechanical seal replacement procedure 5.2.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using the required signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment, remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; its mass exceeds the 25 kg lifting-control threshold. Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the seal and sleeve. The back pull-out design allows the rotating assembly to be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C10",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the withdrawn shaft sleeve for scoring and replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Check bearing grease quantity, inspect the bearings and impeller, and check NPSH to address the documented high-temperature and high-vibration causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial. No sleeve measurement is needed to set the pre-set seal, although the sleeve scoring inspection remains required. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket as required by procedure 5.2 and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace drive-end bearing HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 (6310-C3) together as a pair. Procedure 5.3 requires pair replacement when either bearing shows wear, noise, or high temperature; the reported bearing temperature is high at 84 C against the 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble with lightly oiled threads and tighten the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm, casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm, and bearing-housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm; this bulletin value supersedes the manual's general 25 Nm seal-gland value for this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment after the work, particularly because the bearing housing is disturbed and misalignment is a possible common cause. Apply tolerances of 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, complete the reliability-engineer notification required for Zone D vibration and verify the Plan 11 seal flush arrangement from pump discharge. Do not run the pump dry; investigate the tank-changeover dry-running event before sustained operation.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; mandatory replacement type for this HF-300 serial. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new during the seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; one is required if inspection finds scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with HF3-510 as a bearing pair under procedure 5.3.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with HF3-512 as a bearing pair under procedure 5.3.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediate machinery control: stop the pump because its vibration is in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves, and use a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg threshold: obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is within the P-101 to P-106 filtered-water pump group dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for work on this chemically dosed line.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Raise the work order as priority 1 within the shift because the bearing-housing temperature is above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting HF3-450 and specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000. The bulletin was issued on 14 March 2026 and explicitly covers P-104's serial HF3-22871, so HF3-450B applies to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts and procedure 5.2 generally directs tightening to Table 5, but SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because this asset is within the bulletin's serial range, use 30 Nm for the seal gland nuts; the other applicable Table 5 torques remain 160 Nm for the impeller nut, 210 Nm for casing bolts, and 85 Nm for bearing-housing bolts.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which seal is currently installed, and does the withdrawn shaft sleeve have scoring deeper than 0.1 mm? The installed seal is not stated, and sleeve replacement is conditional on the inspection result.",
    "No numerical allowable shaft-seal leakage rate is supplied, so the approximately one-drop-per-second leakage cannot be classified against a numerical leak-rate limit.",
    "The report does not explicitly state whether the 7.6 mm/s vibration value is RMS, while Figure 3's zones are specified in mm/s RMS. Confirm the measurement basis without delaying the immediate stop required by the reported reading.",
    "Bearing wear/noise findings, grease quantity, impeller condition, alignment measurements, and NPSH/cavitation findings are not supplied; these inspections may identify additional corrective work.",
    "The required bearing grease type and specified quantity are not provided, although the manual requires grease quantity to be checked.",
    "The cause of the 10-minute dry run and the current condition or availability of the Plan 11 seal flush are not documented."
  ]
}
